WEBVTT

00:01.040 --> 00:02.270
<i>The demiplane.</i>

00:02.270 --> 00:06.800
<i>A world created by an unstoppable dragon 
under Misumi Makoto's influence.</i>

00:06.800 --> 00:12.080
<i>As a result, it was populated with Japanese 
flora and fauna, and even savage beasts.</i>

00:14.740 --> 00:19.750
We shall forgive this offense if you 
swear to leave the woods alone.

00:20.460 --> 00:22.530
Just this once. Now leave.

00:22.900 --> 00:25.770
They're letting me go?

00:50.020 --> 00:52.560
<b>Season Two</b>

01:57.120 --> 02:01.010
<b>Night Twelve   Attack of the Giant Monsters</b>

01:57.120 --> 02:01.010
<b>Night Twelve   Attack of the Giant Monsters</b>

01:58.130 --> 01:59.750
A bear and a wolf?

01:59.750 --> 02:04.640
The orcs clearing the woods were 
injured and received a warning.

02:04.640 --> 02:08.770
Since Shiki has returned to the Academy, 
Emma is treating them.

02:08.770 --> 02:12.370
I see. So where were they attacked?

02:12.370 --> 02:13.990
In the woods to the north.

02:14.230 --> 02:15.820
That's nearby.

02:15.820 --> 02:19.530
I wonder if it's related to the 
demiplane's irregular weather changes.

02:20.190 --> 02:25.240
If I make a mist gate in the right place, 
the weather should stabilize, right?

02:25.240 --> 02:27.970
Yes. We're currently looking into it,

02:27.970 --> 02:29.950
but perhaps we should deal 
with these beasts first.

02:29.950 --> 02:32.750
I've heard bear is a delicacy.

02:32.750 --> 02:34.680
Yeah, especially their right paws—

02:34.680 --> 02:36.300
Wait, no!

02:36.300 --> 02:39.830
In some parts of Japan, 
bears are considered holy,

02:39.830 --> 02:43.290
and wolves are the kings of the forest!

02:43.290 --> 02:44.220
Oh, my.

02:44.980 --> 02:50.020
In any case, if we can communicate  
with them, I'm going to go talk to them.

02:50.330 --> 02:53.110
You think rather highly of them.

02:53.110 --> 02:55.970
To me, they're special.

02:56.350 --> 03:00.450
Like the dragons of fantasy 
worlds, I admire them.

03:00.450 --> 03:05.300
If you like dragons, 
there's one right in front of you.

03:05.300 --> 03:09.410
One you wouldn't be embarrassed 
to present anywhere.

03:09.820 --> 03:10.760
Yeah, yeah.

03:11.110 --> 03:14.120
Young Master, what about s-spiders?

03:14.120 --> 03:18.960
S-Spiders are special, too. They eat pests.

03:21.100 --> 03:22.790
Tomoe-san!

03:31.690 --> 03:34.720
<i>If they won't show themselves...</i>

03:38.080 --> 03:39.220
<i>They're close.</i>

03:43.480 --> 03:44.980
It really is a bear.

03:47.710 --> 03:50.040
<i>I'll start by improving my mobility.</i>

03:53.460 --> 03:56.070
<i>I had no idea they were so velvety and soft!</i>

03:56.070 --> 03:58.020
<i>Is it because it's a demiplane bear?</i>

03:59.870 --> 04:01.170
You're wasting your time.

04:06.490 --> 04:08.930
The wolf's out there, too.

04:09.350 --> 04:12.890
I am Misumi Makoto. I'm just here to talk.

04:17.540 --> 04:20.980
<i>Nice. As wolves should be.</i>

04:21.520 --> 04:22.940
Our attacks are ineffective.

04:23.460 --> 04:25.490
There's more than one?

04:26.830 --> 04:30.280
The other day, we sensed an 
extraordinary current of mana.

04:30.950 --> 04:32.750
That was you, wasn't it?

04:32.750 --> 04:34.800
Ah, yeah, probably.

04:34.800 --> 04:37.400
You seem to be the king of this land.

04:37.400 --> 04:40.420
As such, we cannot ignore you.

04:40.420 --> 04:43.570
I'm not interested in ruling over you.

04:43.570 --> 04:47.400
I just came to apologize 
since we're neighbors.

04:47.400 --> 04:48.280
What?

04:49.100 --> 04:52.740
In the future, we won't enter these 
woods without contacting you first.

04:52.740 --> 04:56.640
If you need anything, we'll help you.

04:56.640 --> 04:59.230
Despite your overwhelming strength,

04:59.230 --> 05:02.850
you'll share your territory 
with us and even protect us?

05:02.850 --> 05:05.460
Not protect. Coexist.

05:05.460 --> 05:09.220
I'd like you to continue defending 
these woods like you always have.

05:09.810 --> 05:11.900
I don't get it.

05:12.320 --> 05:15.620
How does that benefit you?

05:16.030 --> 05:20.330
Benefit me? I just want to be friends.

05:20.330 --> 05:21.840
Friends?

05:22.260 --> 05:26.610
With you, these woods, and that bear, too.

05:37.370 --> 05:40.730
You gotta laugh at that, wolf.

05:40.730 --> 05:42.990
<i>H-He's freaking enormous!</i>

05:42.990 --> 05:45.030
Sorry for interrupting.

05:45.790 --> 05:48.530
I'm impressed.

05:49.030 --> 05:52.250
Feel free to call me Brownie.

05:52.250 --> 05:55.200
<i>Brownie? Because he's a brown bear?</i>

05:55.200 --> 05:57.710
Very well, Misumi Makoto.

05:57.710 --> 06:00.740
We accept your kindness and 
agree to become your friends.

06:01.360 --> 06:05.210
We will rule over these woods, 
free from your control.

06:05.790 --> 06:07.480
Are we agreed?

06:07.480 --> 06:09.170
Y-Yeah, of course.

06:09.700 --> 06:13.940
He's an interesting fellow. I'm not sure 
if the one in the sky will accept it.

06:13.940 --> 06:15.630
Don't mind him.

06:15.630 --> 06:19.640
If he needs to get involved, 
he'll show himself.

06:19.640 --> 06:22.840
I suppose you're right. Now, then...

06:22.840 --> 06:23.850
Right.

06:24.380 --> 06:27.560
We look forward to working with you, sir.

06:28.050 --> 06:29.520
Likewise.

06:29.950 --> 06:35.500
<i>And so, a sanctuary known as the Wolf's 
Woods was established in the demiplane.</i>

06:37.100 --> 06:38.960
You can't help that they're your favorite.

06:39.510 --> 06:42.440
But you can't keep picking 
every one you come across.

06:42.440 --> 06:43.350
Okay.

06:43.350 --> 06:44.930
We're sorry.

06:45.190 --> 06:48.340
In Japan, we have something 
called tree-tending persimmons.

06:48.340 --> 06:52.200
Instead of picking every permission 
from a tree that bears lots of fruit,

06:52.200 --> 06:56.680
you leave a few behind to pray for a bountiful 
harvest next year, and for other creatures to—

06:56.680 --> 06:58.330
Hold it!

06:58.800 --> 07:01.990
But this one is surely sweet!

07:01.450 --> 07:03.270
Young Master, look!

07:04.970 --> 07:07.070
Okay, that's freaking enormous!

07:07.070 --> 07:09.160
Its size is impressive.

07:09.710 --> 07:10.370
But...

07:10.960 --> 07:14.100
Anyone who dares to blot out 
the Young Master's sky—

07:14.100 --> 07:15.260
Hold.

07:16.070 --> 07:18.780
I simply came to introduce 
myself to your king.

07:18.780 --> 07:21.220
The wolves told me what happened.

07:21.220 --> 07:23.110
Oh, so you know them.

07:23.110 --> 07:25.710
Indeed. I'll be down shortly.

07:27.930 --> 07:30.870
So it's a fantastical creature after all.

07:30.870 --> 07:34.750
There's no telling what else 
is hiding in the demiplane.

07:34.750 --> 07:36.730
Your world never ceases to amaze me.

07:36.730 --> 07:39.430
It's your world, too.

07:39.430 --> 07:43.740
Besides, there aren't any fantastical 
creatures in Japan. Allegedly.

07:43.740 --> 07:46.990
Which makes it our child.

07:48.440 --> 07:51.590
And the demiplane Komoe's older sister.

07:51.590 --> 07:54.610
The demiplane is my sister?

07:54.610 --> 07:56.950
Komoe-chan, don't take her seriously.

07:58.660 --> 08:00.540
May I?

08:00.540 --> 08:01.570
He's tiny!

08:01.920 --> 08:04.680
I shall speak to you in this form.

08:04.680 --> 08:08.210
Nice to meet you. My name is Misumi Makoto.

08:08.210 --> 08:12.820
I am the Boulder Bird, 
ruler of the skies and mountains.

08:12.820 --> 08:14.180
It's a pleasure to meet you.

08:14.180 --> 08:16.340
Boulder Bird?

08:16.600 --> 08:20.310
<b>Boulder Bird</b>

08:16.640 --> 08:19.840
I've heard of rocs before, but...

08:17.600 --> 08:20.310
<b>Stone Bird</b>

08:18.600 --> 08:20.310
<b>Roc Bird</b>

08:20.620 --> 08:24.890
Going forward, I intend to 
watch the skies for you.

08:24.890 --> 08:27.020
If you have any ideas, 
I'd like to hear them.

08:27.380 --> 08:32.180
Personally, I have no problem with 
you doing what you always have.

08:32.180 --> 08:33.490
I appreciate that.

08:33.490 --> 08:35.780
I do have one request.

08:36.440 --> 08:41.270
Could I perhaps assume that 
"roc" name you mentioned?

08:41.730 --> 08:43.450
I seem to like it.

08:43.450 --> 08:45.640
Uh... Y-Yes, of course.

08:45.640 --> 08:46.730
Thank you.

08:46.730 --> 08:50.030
From now on, I shall call myself Roc Bird.

08:54.850 --> 08:57.770
I feel like I've gained more followers.

08:57.770 --> 09:01.360
Those who haven't formed contracts 
with you can't be called followers.

09:01.930 --> 09:04.840
It would be more appropriate 
to call them subjects.

09:05.730 --> 09:08.440
I see. You're jealous.

09:08.440 --> 09:10.060
Wh-What?

09:10.060 --> 09:11.900
But you're right. 
That was thoughtless of me.

09:12.530 --> 09:16.390
My only followers are Tomoe, Mio, and Shiki.

09:18.820 --> 09:21.880
A-As long as you understand...

09:22.410 --> 09:23.770
Shall we head back?

09:24.360 --> 09:26.490
Komoe-chan, I'll carry half the baskets.

09:26.490 --> 09:28.330
Oh, no. I can do it myself.

09:28.930 --> 09:31.810
I'll show that huge bird who's boss.

09:33.170 --> 09:34.820
<i>It looks like the baskets are walking.</i>

09:37.890 --> 09:39.160
<i>With the setting sun,</i>

09:39.160 --> 09:40.580
<i>it begins to feel like fall</i>

09:40.580 --> 09:41.820
<i>as summer winds down.</i>

09:43.860 --> 09:45.690
Sorry. Thanks for waiting.

09:45.690 --> 09:47.900
It's fine. I didn't wait long.

09:48.370 --> 09:49.680
Anyway, this is unusual.

09:50.130 --> 09:52.580
You rarely want to go for drinks together.

09:52.580 --> 09:54.250
Well, you know.

09:57.810 --> 10:00.570
What? Shiki-san took you?

10:00.570 --> 10:01.370
Yeah.

10:01.370 --> 10:04.070
Seriously? I'm so jealous.

10:04.460 --> 10:07.400
So, what's Shiki-san's type?

10:07.750 --> 10:09.410
That's the first thing you're asking?

10:10.230 --> 10:13.140
He's the type of person to 
order all kinds of drinks.

10:13.140 --> 10:17.130
No, I meant what do his preferred 
type of women drink?

10:17.130 --> 10:18.600
Yeah, yeah.

10:19.990 --> 10:24.110
Come to think of it, we've never had 
the chance to speak like this before.

10:24.110 --> 10:26.460
We both had our hands full.

10:26.940 --> 10:30.510
Scholarship students are tossed 
out if their grades fall.

10:30.510 --> 10:32.680
We were more like rivals than friends.

10:35.430 --> 10:36.580
The truth is...

10:39.150 --> 10:40.850
It's okay. You go first.

10:41.150 --> 10:44.660
There's something I want to 
do before summer break ends.

10:45.230 --> 10:48.330
I want to defeat the demidragon.

10:49.140 --> 10:51.960
If it were hopeless, then I 
could easily admit defeat.

10:52.380 --> 10:53.630
But that...

10:54.530 --> 10:56.920
That was a battle we could've won.

10:57.530 --> 10:58.800
You think so, too?

10:58.800 --> 11:00.880
I'm sure the others are frustrated, too.

11:01.280 --> 11:03.860
Then our last summer activity will be...

11:04.490 --> 11:05.800
It's decided.

11:05.800 --> 11:08.350
Well, I feel better now.

11:09.630 --> 11:13.670
Come to think of it, why did 
you come to the academy?

11:13.670 --> 11:15.000
Were you scouted after all?

11:15.000 --> 11:16.870
Yeah. You, too, right?

11:17.290 --> 11:22.860
I suppose, but frankly, until I met 
Kuzunoha-sensei, I wasn't getting anywhere.

11:23.720 --> 11:25.820
Honestly, same.

11:26.270 --> 11:29.240
So, you're not going back home?

11:29.240 --> 11:31.580
I don't really have one.

11:32.070 --> 11:37.190
It was just me and my mom, 
and my mom died in an epidemic.

11:38.330 --> 11:42.010
It's not like you've gone home, either. 
Is there some reason for that?

11:42.960 --> 11:44.970
Something like that.

11:46.360 --> 11:50.930
There was someone way stronger than 
me in the village I was born in.

11:51.270 --> 11:52.340
Miranda...

11:52.800 --> 11:57.900
She was an orphan forced to fight 
monsters and handle other tough jobs.

11:59.230 --> 12:03.850
And she kept on fighting like she 
was conquering that injustice.

12:04.790 --> 12:07.320
So she's your master?

12:08.070 --> 12:09.100
No.

12:11.160 --> 12:12.880
She was my first love.

12:15.910 --> 12:17.540
Your first love?

12:18.270 --> 12:21.280
Eventually I started helping her.

12:21.280 --> 12:22.470
But one day,

12:22.470 --> 12:26.330
the village ordered us to investigate 
the forbidden forest.

12:27.140 --> 12:28.590
Seriously...

12:29.110 --> 12:33.100
Like we really need to develop 
these creepy woods. Right?

12:35.060 --> 12:37.740
Not very sociable, are you?

12:42.030 --> 12:42.910
Whoa.

12:42.910 --> 12:45.040
Is this a mage's workshop?

12:47.490 --> 12:48.700
Miranda?

13:08.120 --> 13:09.650
M-Miranda...

13:09.650 --> 13:10.880
Run!

13:36.610 --> 13:37.820
Miranda...

13:39.820 --> 13:42.270
Y-You're a monster.

13:45.060 --> 13:47.820
That was the last time I saw her.

13:49.840 --> 13:54.100
I couldn't forgive the village I grew 
up in, or my own powerlessness.

13:54.700 --> 13:59.180
So I honed my skills and jumped on the 
academy's offer when they scouted me.

14:00.170 --> 14:03.660
I wanted to find Miranda and 
apologize to her someday.

14:05.080 --> 14:10.000
I wanted to become as strong as 
her and tell her I was sorry.

14:12.020 --> 14:14.110
That's one hell of a reason.

14:14.400 --> 14:19.490
So I guess that demidragon is the 
first obstacle you have to overcome.

14:19.490 --> 14:21.640
More or less.

14:22.420 --> 14:23.450
What?

14:23.450 --> 14:25.270
A rematch against the demidragon?

14:25.270 --> 14:29.200
Yes. Jin and his merry band 
want to fight it again,

14:29.200 --> 14:30.950
without your knowledge.

14:30.950 --> 14:31.920
I see.

14:32.200 --> 14:35.850
Do they think I'd be angry if I found out?

14:35.850 --> 14:38.210
At their age, kids want to push themselves.

14:38.210 --> 14:42.560
But the Rembrandt sisters 
went home, didn't they?

14:42.560 --> 14:45.100
Lime reported on that.

14:45.100 --> 14:46.320
Lime did?

14:46.320 --> 14:47.320
Yes.

14:47.880 --> 14:53.980
He was watching over the sisters in Tsige 
and even provided them with a place to train.

14:53.980 --> 14:55.270
Wait, what?

14:55.630 --> 15:00.350
They've currently returned to Rotsgard and 
are working on a plan with the other students.

15:00.350 --> 15:01.260
I see.

15:01.800 --> 15:05.800
At their current level, I doubt 
they'd lose to a demidragon.

15:05.800 --> 15:07.510
Then let's leave them be.

15:07.510 --> 15:09.990
We won't have Eris watch 
over them this time.

15:09.990 --> 15:14.720
Not so fast. There's a pack of demidragons 
gathered around that watering hole.

15:14.720 --> 15:15.960
A whole pack?

15:15.960 --> 15:18.680
Isn't seeing just one of them unusual?

15:18.680 --> 15:20.600
I can't imagine it's a coincidence.

15:21.220 --> 15:24.810
If you'll allow it, 
I'd like to investigate the area.

15:24.810 --> 15:28.320
Do it. As for the students...

15:28.790 --> 15:33.660
The kids will look for the demidragon 
where they last encountered it, so...

15:33.660 --> 15:35.860
We should leave one there.

15:36.320 --> 15:38.440
I'll handle the pack.

15:38.440 --> 15:40.220
I'd like to test my mana matter, too.

15:40.220 --> 15:41.870
You'll handle them yourself?

15:42.310 --> 15:44.650
A prayer for the demidragons.

15:48.430 --> 15:52.190
This ritual... Could it be a sacred treasure?

15:53.060 --> 15:57.650
The sacred treasure of Elysion, 
the Scepter of Dragons.

15:57.990 --> 16:01.700
I thought it was lost when 
the nation was destroyed.

16:02.510 --> 16:05.070
<i>Young Master, do you have a moment?</i>

16:05.070 --> 16:06.350
<i>Did you learn something?</i>

16:06.670 --> 16:10.830
<i>Have you seen any altars or 
bloodstains where you are?</i>

16:10.830 --> 16:13.660
<i>You found some, too?</i>

16:13.660 --> 16:18.610
<i>Yes. Someone seems to have conducted 
a ritual to activate a sacred treasure.</i>

16:18.610 --> 16:21.550
<i>Then the demidragons were summoned.</i>

16:21.550 --> 16:24.710
<i>This seems like something demons would do.</i>

16:25.480 --> 16:27.320
<i>Proceed with your investigation.</i>

16:27.620 --> 16:29.990
<i>I'll take care of the pack of demidragons.</i>

16:29.990 --> 16:31.310
<i>Understood.</i>

16:32.920 --> 16:34.260
Now, then...

16:34.260 --> 16:38.220
I'll start by removing one 
for the students' rematch.

16:38.220 --> 16:39.720
That one will do.

16:41.690 --> 16:43.380
<i>Okay. That just leaves...</i>

16:44.950 --> 16:49.500
<i>Even though I can't use wind magic, 
this allows me to travel through the air.</i>

17:06.440 --> 17:08.510
Their breath attacks are ineffective, too.

17:09.260 --> 17:11.330
It's even stronger than I expected.

17:12.540 --> 17:17.000
I don't have anything against 
you guys, but sorry.

17:18.710 --> 17:21.170
Just some resistance fighters.

17:21.170 --> 17:24.770
I heard the current demon lord 
was an exceptional leader.

17:24.770 --> 17:27.700
I'm surprised there are 
those who oppose him.

17:27.700 --> 17:32.180
W-We hate him <i>because</i> 
he's an exceptional king.

17:32.660 --> 17:36.620
That's just how... organizations... are...

17:37.020 --> 17:41.570
In the end, they fled with the sacred 
treasure, and I uncovered no details.

17:41.920 --> 17:44.640
<i>The information I have is still uncertain.</i>

17:45.170 --> 17:51.450
<i>I can't report to the young master yet 
when I don't have the full picture.</i>

17:51.750 --> 17:55.740
Now, I should harvest some of 
the demidragon meat Mio asked for.

17:56.720 --> 17:59.100
I've gotten pretty used to my mana matter.

17:59.100 --> 18:01.630
All that's left is the students' rematch.

18:03.000 --> 18:05.590
Found it. There's only one.

18:05.590 --> 18:08.650
It wasn't there a moment ago. 
Why did it suddenly appear?

18:08.650 --> 18:10.860
It doesn't matter. This suits us just fine.

18:10.860 --> 18:12.580
Battle formation, everyone.

18:12.580 --> 18:14.440
I'll block its roar.

18:14.440 --> 18:15.560
I'll be the vanguard.

18:15.560 --> 18:17.850
Mithra and I will be on the front line.

18:17.850 --> 18:19.170
Daena, stay mobile.

18:19.170 --> 18:21.490
Go all-out, but stay calm.

18:21.490 --> 18:23.540
Right. Let's do what we always do.

18:24.230 --> 18:25.260
Let's go!

18:25.260 --> 18:26.960
Yeah!

18:26.960 --> 18:28.430
Folding Fear!

18:28.750 --> 18:30.050
Triad Muse!

18:30.050 --> 18:32.180
<i>I'll start by boosting defense and mobility.</i>

18:32.430 --> 18:33.630
<i>Then...</i>

18:34.390 --> 18:37.430
Get ready for a real fight, 
you lizard bastard!

18:38.140 --> 18:39.390
It turned to the side!

18:39.390 --> 18:40.200
Get in there!

18:40.200 --> 18:40.840
Got it!

18:40.840 --> 18:41.590
I've got this!

18:47.930 --> 18:48.840
<i>Its breath!</i>

18:49.390 --> 18:50.290
Get back, everyone!

18:55.900 --> 18:59.150
It won't hold. I'll create a barrier, too.

18:59.490 --> 19:01.080
Don't worry. I'll take it.

19:01.080 --> 19:03.530
Grant us a moment's respite.

19:03.530 --> 19:05.350
Di Barrie!

19:09.150 --> 19:11.300
Does that enhancement skill 
absorb breath attacks?

19:11.300 --> 19:13.530
Nice. I've got something, too.

19:14.780 --> 19:17.200
Flames, grant me strength.

19:17.200 --> 19:19.300
Water, grant me wisdom.

19:19.300 --> 19:21.490
Wind, become my path.

19:21.490 --> 19:23.560
Earth, become my clothes.

19:24.680 --> 19:28.400
It boosts everything. 
Mobility, defense, and attack.

19:28.400 --> 19:29.400
I call it...

19:30.530 --> 19:32.410
Ultimate Super Enhancement!

19:33.310 --> 19:35.280
Name aside, that's incredible.

19:35.280 --> 19:37.020
Mithra, let's stop its movements.

19:37.440 --> 19:39.280
Dun ousa riberno.

19:39.770 --> 19:40.820
Aerial!

19:47.130 --> 19:49.700
I'm sick of hearing that roar already!

19:52.740 --> 19:54.720
Stand back, everyone.

19:56.030 --> 19:58.870
This is a combination of 
spirit and elemental magic.

19:58.870 --> 20:02.320
It's the most powerful spell I 
currently have at my disposal.

20:02.960 --> 20:04.630
Don't let it evade her spell, Izumo!

20:04.630 --> 20:06.130
I'll lock it down.

20:35.010 --> 20:38.350
<i>Stronger. I need to become stronger.</i>

20:38.770 --> 20:43.620
<i>I'll continue down this path, 
and find her someday...</i>

20:46.470 --> 20:49.210
Heroes, demons, and wars.

20:49.630 --> 20:52.770
The world continues to move restlessly.

20:52.770 --> 20:58.740
Yes, but in your current state, even 
Kuzunoha is nothing compared to you.

20:58.740 --> 21:01.140
It'd be a problem if he weren't.

21:01.140 --> 21:04.330
Either way, what are you doing here?

21:04.330 --> 21:06.780
No particular reason.

21:07.480 --> 21:13.290
It was here that I once slew a creepy chimera 
with human arms sprouting from its back.

21:13.290 --> 21:14.070
Are you serious?

21:14.070 --> 21:18.470
That's one of the strongest monsters 
used to defend mages' workshops.

21:18.470 --> 21:19.580
I know.

21:19.580 --> 21:24.560
The workshop belonged to Banshoku—to Luto.

21:24.560 --> 21:28.130
I learned my true name here.

21:28.130 --> 21:30.970
It's where I had my start.

21:32.390 --> 21:33.970
Luto of Myriad Colors...

21:34.710 --> 21:36.930
The one who created me.

21:37.580 --> 21:39.690
My parent.

21:41.840 --> 21:42.900
Miranda...

21:44.350 --> 21:46.520
Come to think of it, 
I wonder if he still...

21:47.890 --> 21:51.380
Whatever. I'm not Miranda anymore.

21:53.800 --> 21:55.830
You just wait, Luto.

21:56.290 --> 21:59.330
I'll kill every last greater dragon...

22:00.190 --> 22:02.680
and then I'll consume you.

23:35.310 --> 23:39.690
Night Thirteen: "The Very 
Busy Academy Festival."

23:35.600 --> 23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

23:36.730 --> 23:40.060
<b>The Very Busy Academy Festival</b>
